                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I actually quite enjoyed the game. \nIt`s an RPG maker game (yes, i know. No shit sherlock) and it was developed by an indie developer... Additionally I am a big fan of puzzle games and such stuff which caused me to try this game.\n\nI had no problems solving the puzzles in the early game. Some puzzles are innovative and interesting. Not every puzzle is though (i speak to you: Lights Puzzle), but most of them are. Every game has some weak puzzles. Every puzzle can be figured out logically which makes it fun to progress and proceed through the rooms. The game also has different paths you can take and different endings you can get. Saving, loading and such stuff is no problem, you can do that anytime before important choices.  \n\nI have finished the game, completed all secrets and hidden puzzles. The puzzles in the late-game were really difficult and i had a hard-time figuring them out. The puzzles are great and i definitely would buy this game again for them.\n\nThe big downside is the story though. It`s pretty... weeeird. The story concept is actually not that bad... but [spoiler] come on, the typical Secret Agent plot twist ^^ [/spoiler] thus making the story really mediocre. The dialogue is skippable, which is important for those kind of games (you don`t want to play twice through story sections to reach different endings without being able to skip :p)\n\nAnother thing i like are the hidden puzzles. It`s a good way of including secrets in your game. Some of them are hidden very uncreatively though (at the walls, really?). All in all it`s pretty fun to find them though (some are hidden pretty good!)\n\nYes, due to that i believe I can reccommend the game especially because of the puzzles. The story and dialogue aren`t that good, but it`s not like it`s disturbing the gameplay. The price tag is 6,99 and you get about 10 hours gameplay (yes, i needed that long. Maybe you`re faster... but that`s how long i needed for all endings!). I don`t see anything unfair there, so it`s fine. \n\nThe puzzles are the best reasons why to buy this game. The story is - unfortunately - not that strong.\nYou know, If i ever would have made a game, it would have had a similar concept puzzle-wise like this one ;)",
